  "result": "I found and fixed the bug. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:35` compared the sku it was given against each line's item **name** instead of its **sku**. `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so no line was ever removed.\n\nThe fix compares against the sku instead:\n```python\nself.lines = [l for l in self.lines if l.item.sku != sku]\n```\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, because only the Gadget line is left. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`. All 6 passed.\n\nNone of those tests cover `Cart.remove`, so the suite wouldn't have caught this bug. I can add a test for it if you want.",
